{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And unleavened bread, and unleavened loaves, and unleavened wafers.</b> These are three kinds mingled with oil; the loaves and the wafers are unleavened bread. It is what is called below in the matter (verse 23) חַלַּת לֶחֶם שֶׁמֶן — because oil is put in the mingling corresponding to the loaves and the wafers. And all the kinds come ten by ten loaves." "<b>Mingled with oil.</b> While they are flour he pours oil into them and mingles them." "<b>Anointed with oil.</b> After they are baked he anoints them like a kind of Greek [vessel], which is made like our כְּנוּ\"ן."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:25.280276758Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}